<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31251" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nŏvācŭla</span></b> ,
		ae, f.
		novo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a sharp knife</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cutem raporum novaculā decerpere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					12, 56, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 22, 23, 47, §
			99</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Esp. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>A razor</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut ex novaculā comperistis, tonsor
					est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 103</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aream (capitis) novaculā radere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 6,
					4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nudare caput,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					2, 66, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">secare fauces,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Calig. 23</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 29, 6, 34, § 107</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tarquinius dixit, se cogitāsse, cotem
					novaculā posse praecidi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 1, 17, 32</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Liv. 1, 36</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val. Max. 1,
				4, 1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>A dagger</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stringitur in densā nec caeca
					novacula turbā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					7, 61, 7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>the name of a
			fish</i>, otherwise unknown, <i><span class="en">Plin. 32, 2,
				5, § 14</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
